---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
---

<ContentLayout title="Privacy Policy - PasteDownloadApp" description="Privacy Policy for PasteDownloadApp. Learn how we handle browser-based image processing, analytics, advertising, and cookies." canonicalUrl="https://pastedownloadapp.com/privacy/" breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Home", href: "/" }, { name: "Privacy Policy" }]}>
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "name": "Privacy Policy - PasteDownloadApp",
      "description": "Privacy Policy for PasteDownloadApp. Learn how PasteDownloadApp handles browser-based image processing, analytics, advertising, cookies, and third-party services.",
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "PasteDownloadApp"
      }
    }
  </script>

  <h1 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl lg:text-[28px] font-semibold text-ink tracking-tight mt-0 mb-6 leading-tight text-balance">
    Privacy Policy
  </h1>

  <div class="text-body text-base sm:text-[17px] leading-relaxed space-y-4 [&_h2]:text-ink [&_h2]:text-lg [&_h2]:sm:text-xl [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:tracking-tight [&_h2]:mt-8 [&_h2]:mb-2 [&_h2]:leading-tight [&_h3]:text-ink [&_h3]:text-base [&_h3]:sm:text-lg [&_h3]:font-semibold [&_h3]:tracking-tight [&_h3]:mt-6 [&_h3]:mb-2 [&_h3]:leading-tight [&_a]:text-link [&_a]:underline [&_a]:underline-offset-2 [&_a]:decoration-link/30 [&_a]:transition-colors [&_a:hover]:decoration-link">
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> October 2026</p>

    <h2>Image Processing</h2>
    <p>
      PasteDownloadApp is designed to process images in your browser whenever possible. Images pasted from your clipboard or added by drag and drop are handled locally using browser APIs such as the <strong>Clipboard API</strong> and <strong>Canvas API</strong>. We do <strong>not</strong> upload, store, or have access to images you paste from your device.
    </p>
    <h2>Browser Extension</h2>
    <p>
      The Paste Download browser extension turns the image on your clipboard into a downloaded file. It requests a single permission, <strong>clipboard read access</strong>, which is used only when you press Ctrl+V or Cmd+V, or tap the paste area, in the extension popup. The image is converted and saved on your device using browser APIs. The extension does <strong>not</strong> upload, store, or transmit your images or clipboard contents, does not make network requests, and does not include analytics, advertising, or tracking. It stores only your chosen image format and theme in the extension's local browser storage, and this stays on your device. We do not sell or share any user data, and we do not use it for purposes unrelated to the extension's single purpose.
    </p>
    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>
      We do not require an account and we do not ask you to provide your name, email address, or payment information to use the image tool. We may collect limited technical and usage information through analytics and advertising services, such as pages visited, browser type, device type, approximate location, referrer, interactions, and similar diagnostic information.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your browser may also store a local theme preference so the site can remember whether you prefer light mode or dark mode. This preference is stored locally in your browser and is not used to identify you.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      Our website uses <strong>Google Fonts</strong> for typography. When you load the page, your browser requests font files from Google's servers, which may log your IP address according to Google's privacy policy. We use a <code>preconnect</code> and <code>preload</code> strategy to minimize the impact of this request.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use <strong>Google Analytics</strong> to understand how visitors use the site and to improve the tool. Google Analytics may use cookies or similar technologies to collect usage information.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may use <strong>Google AdSense</strong> or other Google advertising services to display ads. Google and its partners may use cookies, including the <strong>DoubleClick DART cookie</strong>, along with web beacons, IP addresses, advertising identifiers, and similar technologies to serve ads, measure ad performance, prevent fraud, and personalize ads where permitted. The DART cookie enables Google and its partners to serve ads based on your visits to this site and other sites on the Internet. Third-party vendors, including Google, may use cookies such as the DART cookie to serve ads based on your prior visits to this and other websites.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can learn more about how Google uses data from sites that use Google services at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>. You can turn off personalized ads from Google at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ad Settings</a>, and opt out of many third-party vendors' personalized advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a> or, in Europe, <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">youronlinechoices.eu</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Local Storage and Offline Copies</h2>
    <p>
      To remember your choices, the site keeps a few small items in your browser's local storage: your theme, a count of how many images you have downloaded, and when you last dismissed the optional bookmark / install bar. These never leave your device. The site also uses a service worker, which stores copies of the site's own pages and files in your browser so it loads faster and works offline. It only handles requests to pastedownloadapp.com, never to analytics or advertising providers. You can remove all of this by clearing the site's data in your browser. The <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> lists each item.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and Consent</h2>
    <p>
      Cookies and similar technologies may be used for analytics, advertising, security, fraud prevention, frequency capping, and ad measurement. If you visit from the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or Switzerland, a consent message from Google asks for your choice before analytics or advertising cookies, including the DART cookie described above, are set for personalized ads or measurement. You can change your choice at any time using the privacy settings option that Google's message leaves on the page. In other regions, these cookies are allowed by default and you can opt out using the tools linked above. Our <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> lists each cookie the site uses.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Images pasted from your device are processed in your browser session and are not retained by us. Analytics and advertising providers may retain usage, cookie, and ad-related data according to their own retention policies. Local browser preferences remain on your device until you clear your browser data.
    </p>

    <h2>Your Rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, delete, correct, object to, or restrict certain uses of your personal data. You may also be able to withdraw consent for advertising or analytics cookies through your browser settings, consent controls, or Google ad settings. If you have any questions about this privacy policy, please <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> or email <a href="mailto:hello@pastedownloadapp.com">hello@pastedownloadapp.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      Because image processing happens entirely in your browser, the images you paste or download never pass through our servers, which removes an entire category of risk around server-side data breaches. We still recommend keeping your browser up to date, since browser security patches directly affect how safely the Clipboard API and Canvas API handle your data. If you access the site over an untrusted network, such as public Wi-Fi, the usual precautions for any website apply here as well.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      PasteDownloadApp is not directed at children under the age of 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information through analytics or advertising services, please <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> and we will take steps to have it removed.
    </p>

    <h2>International Users</h2>
    <p>
      PasteDownloadApp is accessible worldwide, and the analytics and advertising providers we use may process and store information on servers located outside your country of residence, including in the United States. By using the Service, you understand that your information may be transferred to and processed in countries with data protection laws that differ from those in your own country.
    </p>

    <h2>Do Not Track Signals</h2>
    <p>
      Some browsers offer a &ldquo;Do Not Track&rdquo; setting. There is no common industry standard for how websites should respond to this signal, so PasteDownloadApp does not currently change its behavior based on Do Not Track browser signals. You can still control cookies and ad personalization directly through the links in the Third-Party Services section above, or through your browser's own privacy settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this privacy policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated revision date.
    </p>
  </div>
</ContentLayout>
